    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ae8787eb_b5c889f7",
        "filename": "common/mkbp_event.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 55,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287098
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-27T18:39:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like these are mutually exclusive. If so, could we instead have something like\n\n    #define MKBP_EVENT_DELIVERY_GPIO 1\n    #define MKBP_EVENT_DELIVERY_HOST 2\n\nand here\n\n    #if CONFIG_MKBP_HOST_EVENT_DELIVERY \u003d\u003d MKBP_EVENT_DELIVERY_GPIO\n    // thing 1\n    #elif CONFIG_MKBP_HOST_EVENT_DELIVERY \u003d\u003d ...\n    // other stuff\n    #else\n    #error \"Please define CONFIG_MKBP_HOST_EVENT_DELIVERY\"\n    #endif\n\nThe advantage would be that you can\u0027t accidentally or otherwise define both methods and expect anything to work.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 55,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "c8213e5e3d8a7a9ba290f573375beed7110637bd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eb730878_359edcff",
        "filename": "common/mkbp_event.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 55,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-28T16:06:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This paradigm isn\u0027t used in the EC very much yet, but I do like the approach.\n\nOne potential downside of this approach at least for the EC build system is that we might not have access to the MKBP_EVENT_DELIVERY_GPIO defines values in our build system, where we do have access to CONFIG_MKBP_USE_GPIO and CONFIG_MKBP_USE_HOST_EVENT to include different complication units (which may not be needed in this case though)\n\nIn the EC today, the mutual exclusiveness of config options is done in config.h (see hostcmd_lpc and hostcmd_espi)\n\nI lean toward doing it the way EC already does it today, but I could be swayed",
      "parentUuid": "ae8787eb_b5c889f7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "startChar": 0,
